<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταντ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>come down to, arrive</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὰ
				βασίλεια, ἐπὶ κοίτην</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.27
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				59.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν φυσικὴν ὁδόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					259.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				185.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				251.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in a speech
			or narrative, <i>come to, arrive at</i> a point, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὴν ἔκπτωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.1.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινας λογισμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.37.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐπὶ τὸν ὅρκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.79
				</span></i>
			, cf. J <i><span class="en">
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.10.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>have recourse to</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἡδονήν</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3p.63U.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὰ δάκρυα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					p.62
				</span></i>
			 O. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. εἰς ἑαυτούς</span>
			<i>attack, commence hostilities against</i> each other, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.11.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of events,
				<i>come upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶς δ᾽ ἀγὼν ἐπ᾽ ἐμὲ κατήντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					261.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. εἴς τινα</span>
			<i>affect</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.83
			</span></i> W.; of blood-guiltiness, <i>fall</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ κεφαλήν τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>2 Ki.</u>
					3.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>turn out, result</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῦ καταντήσει πάλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.4.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρᾶγμα κ. εἰς ὑπόνοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸ μηδέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.34.2
				</span></i>
			; so of numbers, <i>to be reduced</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς μόνους ἄνδρας δέκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					903.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> of an inheritance, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. εἴς τινα</span>
			<i>fall</i> to one's share, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
				10.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				75
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans., <i>make to come back, bring back</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Palaeph.
				2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἑαυτὸν τὴν ἀρχιερωσύνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>2 Ma.</u>
					4.24
				</span></i>
			 (so intr. in pf., <i>return</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸν αὐτὸν κατηντηκέναι βίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					1101.5
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
